### Description

Iterating large queue throw exception.

### Reproduction Steps

 ``` c#
 using System.Collections.Generic;
 using System;

 var queue = new Queue <int> ();
 queue.EnsureCapacity(Array.MaxLength);
 for (var i = 0; i < Array.MaxLength - 2; i++) {
   queue.Enqueue(i);
   queue.Dequeue();
 }
 for (var i = 0; i < Int32.MaxValue - Array.MaxLength + 4; i++) {
   queue.Enqueue(i);
 }

 var latest = 0;
 foreach(var i in queue) {
   latest = i;
 }
 Console.WriteLine(latest);

```

### Expected behavior

Do not throws exception.

### Actual behavior

```
Unhandled exception. System.IndexOutOfRangeException: Index was outside the bounds of the array.
   at System.Collections.Generic.Queue`1.Enumerator.MoveNext()
```

